# The Electoral Reform Society's own worked "model election" from the 3rd edition of "How to
# conduct an election by the Single Transferable Vote" (the ERS97 rulebook itself): 11
# candidates, 6 seats, 753 valid votes. Ballot-level data reconstructed and verified against
# the rulebook's own hand-computed count sheet by Lee Yingtong Li, bundled as a correctness
# test fixture (tests/data/ers97.blt + tests/data/ers97.csv) in pyRCV2
# (https://yingtongli.me/git/pyRCV2, GNU AGPLv3) -- an independent, third-party STV
# implementation. This is that same file, converted to add the trailing "0" ballot terminator
# our BltParser requires (pyRCV2's own BLT reader doesn't need it).
#
# Cross-checked against the rulebook's own count sheet (as reproduced in pyRCV2's
# tests/data/ers97.csv): quota 107.58, first preferences Smith 134 / Duke 105 / Prince 91 /
# Freeman 90 / Carpenter 81 / Baron 64 / Abbot 59 / Vicar 55 / Wright 27 / Glazier 24 / Monk
# 23; Smith elected stage 1 (surplus 26.42). Round 2 (after Smith's surplus is transferred)
# matches the rulebook's stage 2 exactly for every candidate. Round 3 (after Monk is fully
# eliminated) matches the rulebook's stage 4 exactly, including Duke's tally of 108.68 -- this
# specifically exercises the "exclusion by value, largest value-group first, with newly
# quota-crossing candidates frozen mid-elimination" rule (see
# info.fkhodkov.rankedchoice.stv.StvCounter's class javadoc): Duke crosses quota partway
# through Monk's elimination and must stop receiving votes from its remaining, lower-valued
# groups. Final result: Smith, Duke, Carpenter, Prince, Freeman, and Vicar elected, matching
# the rulebook.
#
# Ers97ModelElectionFixtureTest replays the whole count against the rulebook's count sheet
# (ers97-model-election.rulebook.txt): every round matches one of its stages.
